{"description":"Design: docs/design/conditional.md. Decisions: docs/design/DECISIONS.md.
Note key: C5. Crates: jmap-server (push.rs, tests). Size: S.

Implement the PushSubscription part of docs/design/conditional.md §5.1 and §9 emailpush paragraph (conditional-02 §2.1, §9.1; RFC 8620 §7.2.2). Decisions 1 and 17 (docs/design/DECISIONS.md): add the separate attach call register_push_subscription_conditional<B: PushSubscriptionBackend + ConditionalBackend>(dispatcher, backend), made after register_push_subscription_handlers, attaching SetSupport to the one registered PushSubscription/set through Dispatcher::attach_set_support; it does not re-register the method, and register_push_subscription_handlers is unchanged. SetScopeRequest.account_id = None (scope keyed by credentials). Decision 16: PushSubscriptionBackend has no check_push_subscription_change hook; extension validation (EmailPush check_email_push_change, chatPush validate_chat_push) runs inside the backend's create_/update_push_subscription, so it runs inside the begin_set scope and nothing can drop it last-wins. Lands after the emailpush push.rs seam (emailpush E1, JMAP-r44n.6). Acceptance: mock-backend tests (serialized_writes_scope): precondition on keys or url -> forbidden (PushSubscription/get already forbids them); ifInState still ignored (no /get state); a precondition on a readable property passes and fails as specified; conditional_ready() true with push + probe registered and opted in; under atomic, a SetError from the mock's create_push_subscription (standing in for extension validation, decision 16) gives atomicFailure and nothing is stored; public-api additions only.","notes":"2026-11-13: updated for decisions 16 and 17","title":"jmap-server push: register_push_subscription_conditional attach call (no validation hook)"}
